  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Huntington Ingalls has $3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 71 awards. Huntington Ingalls has an average award size of $42.9M and obligations are down 27.4% year over year. Huntington Ingalls concentrates federal work in Ship Building and Repairing, which accounts for $2.9B of obligations in FY2026 to date. Huntington Ingalls also records obligations in Engineering Services and Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance, at $58.4M and $47.1M respectively, and smaller recorded obligations in Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing at $7.5M and Hardware Manufacturing at $0. The FY26 totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date activity. Historical context shows obligations of $3.6B in FY21, $3B in FY22, $3.2B in FY23, $3.6B in FY24, and $4.2B in FY25, with the FY26 figure matching the FY22 total at $3B.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did Huntington Ingalls obligations fall year over year?",
        "body": "Huntington Ingalls obligations fell 27.4% year over year. Huntington Ingalls FY2026 to date obligations are $3B compared with prior-year levels reflected in the historical series. Huntington Ingalls had peak obligations of $4.2B in FY25, which provides context for the drop to $3B in FY26 to date. Huntington Ingalls FY26 total is a partial fiscal year figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do Huntington Ingalls obligations go by industry?",
        "body": "Ship Building and Repairing is the largest market for Huntington Ingalls at $2.9B in FY2026 to date. Huntington Ingalls also records $58.4M in Engineering Services and $47.1M in Other Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance. Huntington Ingalls records smaller obligations in Power Boiler and Heat Exchanger Manufacturing at $7.5M and Hardware Manufacturing at $0."
      }
    ]
